 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Cleaning them with a soft brush under running water is usually enough. If they' really stuck, you can use a little toothpaste. That's too long. They start to oxidise and lose their bounce. Keep them dry between uses. You can try using a little bit of heat from a hairdryer and then wash them. If that doesn't work, they may be beyond rescue. Then buy new ones. Luster brushes are cheap and they last for years.",
